# Lanes `fleet-bench retro` canaries beside the claude lane each week: `harness model [effort]`, one a line.
# A lane runs only when the source its harness spends from (harnesses.json `source`) has room; a claude
# lane, when a Claude account has. An effort overrides the harness's own default for that lane's runs;
# with none, the harness's default. A claude lane names one, which keeps it out of the claude baseline.
# A harness with a `projects` allowlist replays only those projects' tasks (ocfree: public input only).
# A canary is the score that can lift a harness's `max_tier` (harnesses.json): go, nim and ocfree take tier-1
# work only until their canaries score beside the claude lane's.
codex sol medium
codex sol high
claude haiku max
claude sonnet medium
ocfree beam
opencode-go glm
nim deepseek
